.Dd March 27, 2026
.Dt TVG-SVG2PNG 1
.Os thorvg
.Sh NAME
.Nm tvg-svg2png
.Nd convert SVG files to PNG images
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar SVG-file ...
.Op Ar SVG-folder
.Op Fl r Ar resolution
.Op Fl b Ar bgColor
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
converts SVG (Scalable Vector Graphics) files to PNG raster images
using the ThorVG rendering engine.
.Pp
When given a directory, it recursively processes all
.Pa .svg
files found within.
.Pp
In the case where the width and height in the SVG file determine
the size of the image in resolution higher than 8K (7680 x 4320),
limiting the resolution to this value is enforced while preserving
the aspect ratio.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl r Ar WIDTHxHEIGHT
Set the output image resolution in pixels
.Pq e.g., Fl r Ar 200x200 .
If not specified, the SVG's intrinsic dimensions are used.
.It Fl b Ar HEXCOLOR
Set the output image background color as a hexadecimal value
without the
.Ql #
prefix
.Pq e.g., Fl b Ar ff00ff No for magenta .
Defaults to
.Ar ffffff
(white).
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Convert a single SVG file:
.Pp
.Dl $ tvg-svg2png input.svg
.Pp
Convert with a specific resolution and background color:
.Pp
.Dl $ tvg-svg2png input.svg -r 200x200 -b ff00ff
.Pp
Convert multiple SVG files:
.Pp
.Dl $ tvg-svg2png input1.svg input2.svg -r 200x200 -b ff00ff
.Pp
Convert all SVG files in the current directory:
.Pp
.Dl $ tvg-svg2png \&. -r 200x200
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr tvg-lottie2gif 1
